@title Month-end close runbook
@subtitle Close the books within 5 working days
@author Tallow & Brook Distribution, Controller
@date 2026-10-01

kpi Close target | 5 working days | goal | neutral
kpi Books lock | Day 5, 12:00 | no posting after | bad
kpi Reconciling difference | < $50 | or explained | neutral
kpi Variance needing explanation | > 5% and > $10,000 | written | neutral

!!! The books lock at 12:00 on day 5. Nothing is posted after that without an approved reopen request signed by the Controller.

# Calendar
step Cut off sales and purchasing at 17:00; finish bank reconciliations | Day 1 | Accounting staff
step Post accruals and depreciation; reconcile inventory to the warehouse count | Day 2 | Accounting staff
step Eliminate intercompany balances between the three legal entities; reconcile payroll | Day 3 | Accounting staff
step Review variances | Day 4 | Accounting staff
step Controller signs off; books lock at 12:00 | Day 5 | Marcus Eldridge

# Before sign-off
- [ ] Every balance sheet account is reconciled.
- [ ] Any reconciling difference is under $50 or explained.
- [ ] Variances over 5% and over $10,000 each have a written explanation.
- [ ] Intercompany balances net to zero.
- [ ] Trial balance debits equal credits.

# If a deadline slips
1. Tell the Controller the same day.
2. Decide whether the slip delays sign-off. If day 5 will be missed by more than 1 working day, notify the CFO, Valentina Sokolov.
3. Do not post late entries after the lock without a reopen request signed by the Controller.
4. Record the cause in the close log.

# Contacts
table = role,name; Controller,Marcus Eldridge; Accounts payable lead,Noor Haddad; CFO,Valentina Sokolov
